{"requirements":[{"id":"daily-rotation","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed rule specifies daily rotation, is loaded by the main logrotate configuration, and the enabled active timer shows its next daily run. A forced rotation also completed successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7b64abcc798a4e07","cmd-a6ea45f7ea3243de","cmd-3fb27e02b4454961","cmd-ff6f96a5eedb4c68"]},{"id":"retention-compression","requirement":"Keep seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The rule specifies rotate 7 with immediate compression. A real rotation produced a valid gzip archive, and logrotate reported a rotation count of seven.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7b64abcc798a4e07","cmd-a6ea45f7ea3243de","cmd-2f1fe91a8f254d7f","cmd-3fb27e02b4454961"]},{"id":"write-continuity","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"During a bounded live-writer test, copytruncate preserved the live file and writer descriptor inode. The archive ended at marker 30 while subsequent writes reached marker 40 in the live log, directly demonstrating continued writing after rotation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8cd1ca3dad724a16","cmd-a6ea45f7ea3243de","cmd-2f1fe91a8f254d7f"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the logrotate rule was the required implementation; the temporary writer, forced rotation, and temporary-file cleanup were bounded functional evidence; and the reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. Temporary test files were removed, no failed services or new network exposure remained, and package health stayed clean after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7b64abcc798a4e07","cmd-8cd1ca3dad724a16","cmd-a6ea45f7ea3243de","cmd-2f1fe91a8f254d7f","cmd-af33328d49584e68","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The rule is persistent and scheduled daily, specifies seven immediately compressed rotations, successfully produced a valid compressed archive, and directly demonstrated uninterrupted writing across rotation. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also complete: pre-restart identity and health were captured, restart was acknowledged and disruption observed, the boot identity changed, and the system, timer, rule, live data, and archive recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Retention through seven complete rotation cycles and eviction of an eighth archive was not directly exercised; the conclusion relies on the installed rotate 7 rule and logrotate's reported behavior.","The continuity test used a synthetic writer rather than a named production application process, although it directly tested the required open-file writing behavior."]}
